# sncosmo_models, every template whose source parameter is a bare amplitude.
# Used for anything --sncosmo-model names except the SALT family.
#
# redback ships no prior for sncosmo_models. amplitude here is a RAW flux
# normalisation, not the normalised amplitude of redback's
# sn1998bw_template.prior where 1.0 is SN 1998bw itself, so no range could be
# copied. Derived with sncosmo's own set_source_peakabsmag, spanning M_peak in
# (-14, -22) over z in (0.001, 3), for every non-SALT template.
#
# redshift runs from 0.01, the lower bound of redback's own
# sn1998bw_template.prior, to 3, the upper bound it gives its supernova
# models. It is sampled
# only when neither --z-known nor --z-phot is given; either of those replaces it
# with a DeltaFunction or a TruncatedGaussian at run time. The fit also
# truncates it to the template's spectral validity for the bands in the data
# file, which cannot be known here.
redshift = Uniform(minimum=0.01, maximum=3, name='redshift', latex_label='$z$')
amplitude = LogUniform(minimum=1.399e-22, maximum=3.567e-02, name='amplitude', latex_label='$A$')
